WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.069
Re your article 'More shopping Sundays?'

00:00:04.319 --> 00:00:06.715
Dear Sir or Madam,

00:00:06.965 --> 00:00:26.864
In your article, a businessman calls for shops in the city centre to be allowed to open on Sundays too. He thinks that many people have no time to shop during the week and that otherwise the shops will lose out to online retail. I understand this argument, but I still disagree.

00:00:27.114 --> 00:00:49.133
I have worked as a sales assistant in a department store for twelve years. I already work every other Saturday, often until eight in the evening. For me and my colleagues, Sunday is the only day when the whole family is together. If the shops open, we will have to work — and our children will see us even less.

00:00:49.383 --> 00:01:09.499
Besides, I don't believe that more will really be bought. People don't have more money just because shops are open longer. They simply spread their shopping over more days. A quiet Sunday is not a luxury but a piece of quality of life for everyone — customers included.

00:01:09.749 --> 00:01:13.433
Yours sincerely,
Petra Lorenz, Dresden
